WEBVTT

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:05.110
I see.

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:08.760
So you saw the device under Mt. Sankaku?

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:15.000
I would've preferred to
tell you about Ryuzoji in writing,

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:20.610
but at the time, I didn't know
that he was actually something else.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:34.110
I'm back.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.810
Hello?

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:56.650
Mitsuki-<i>san</i>?

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:00.670
Takuya? Why are you calling so late?

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:04.370
I just really wanted to hear your voice...

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:07.040
What?

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:10.460
That's why you're calling me
in the middle of the night?

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:13.170
Yeah. That's the only reason.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:16.840
I think my heart skipped a beat.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:19.510
It reminded me of old times...

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:25.540
Takuya, you sound tired.

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:30.880
You know better than anybody that I've
got the endurance to keep going on forever.

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:35.480
If you can tell jokes like that,
it means you're probably okay, huh?

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:36.970
Yeah.

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:38.770
Talk to you later.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:49.750
Ryuzoji...

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:52.880
What are you after?

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:31.890
"Episode 12: The Secret Under the White Coat"

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:33.950
This is your wake-up call!

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:38.980
--Your superhero in your hour of need,
Masakatsu Yuki, is here!

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:39.860
--My superhero in my hour of need,
Masakatsu Yuki, is here, huh?

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:42.860
Boss, how did you know
what I was going to say?

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:45.910
Are we bound by the red thread of fate?

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:49.500
Forget that. You know
a lot about the curse, right?

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:51.740
Yes.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:56.500
Do you know when Ryuzoji
moved into that mansion?

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:03.360
Oh, I think by the time everybody started
talking about the curse, he'd moved in.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:04.880
I see.

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:07.850
You do know a lot. Thanks.

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:09.430
Ask me about anything!

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:11.850
The lightning strikes, rumors...

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:13.750
You sound happy.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:16.810
That's right.

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:19.950
I'm looking into it all for Shimazu-<i>san</i>...

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:21.860
Time for class!

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:27.370
Since I'm a nice guy,
I'll ask you to do my work for me again.

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:29.490
What?

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:32.580
Don't you want to do
the same work Mio's doing?

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:33.210
Never mind.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:34.000
I do!

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:35.540
I'd love to do your work for you!

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:38.420
I'd like nothing more in the world!

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:39.590
Right?

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:43.590
Okay, I'll let you do
my work for me again, then!

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:44.750
Thank you!

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:51.620
I'll see you later, Mom.

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:54.180
Goodbye.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:01.480
So Ryuzoji moved into
that mansion the same time

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:04.860
the rumors about the curse started, huh?

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:09.870
At this point, that doesn't
seem like a coincidence.

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:18.770
I could try confronting him directly,
but that Niarb is tough to handle.

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:22.500
What separates it from regular hypnosis

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:26.040
is that your normal
consciousness remains awake.

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:29.260
It's a state of hypnosis
where since you're awake,

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:32.570
you don't realize you're being controlled.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:37.600
Eriko-<i>sensei</i> may know a way to deal with it.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:41.070
Eriko-<i>sensei</i>!

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:43.770
She's not here?

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:47.560
Man, she's never around.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.160
Her clothes are on the bed again!

00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:58.750
They're still warm.

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:00.300
So the suspect is still nearby...

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.060
Eriko-<i>sensei</i>?

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:07.070
Where is she?

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:19.700
I don't know how she
can sleep on this hard floor.

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:22.480
How do you sleep?

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:24.470
On the floor.

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:27.270
Is that the new thing?

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:34.190
Abel... Del... Midra...

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:39.670
Abel! It's so hot... the flames...

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:41.130
Abel!

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:44.560
Are you okay, Eriko-<i>sensei</i>?

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:49.680
Don't leave me.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:53.760
I swear I'll find them and...

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:03.160
Abel...

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:10.360
This is, um... well...

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:13.990
Abel!

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:16.820
You came back!

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:19.830
Abel...

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:22.570
Eriko-<i>sensei</i>!

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:24.380
Snap out of it!

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:28.880
Huh? You're...

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:32.470
Hello. I'm Arima.

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:40.740
Did you see that special--

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:42.810
That voice!

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:44.110
It came from the nurse's office!

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:47.430
--What's wrong?!
--Eriko-<i>sensei</i>!

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:53.960
What are you doing?

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:56.200
Arima!

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:00.500
I'm sorry. It seems I 
gave you the wrong idea.

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:02.920
You just <i>happened</i>
to walk into the nurse's office,

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:06.230
where she just <i>happened</i> to be changing?

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:09.210
Was it really a coincidence, I wonder?

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:11.840
Shimazu-<i>san</i>, you should trust me more--

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:12.770
What did you say?

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:16.610
Nothing. No.

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:20.560
Sensei! They made this boy by
sticking arms and legs on a libido,

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:23.520
and covering it with the skin of a pervert!

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:25.190
Be careful!

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:26.860
That's pretty mean...

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:29.320
But I'm right, aren't I?

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:31.510
You've got a track record.

00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:33.070
A track record?

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:34.320
What's she talking about?

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:36.610
Um, nothing big.

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:42.450
What do you intend to do with that thing?

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:45.670
I can't imagine you want 
it for financial gain.

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:48.250
Pure academic curiosity?

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:50.920
Don't ask too many questions.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:52.460
It's not good for either of us.

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:54.590
I'm aware of that.

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:58.010
I was just a little curious...

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:06.680
Why would someone like you
be willing to take risks like this?

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:09.730
Oh, Yuki!

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:11.070
What's that video?

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:12.990
A special on the
paranormal they did last night!

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:15.110
It was all about the curse!

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:16.750
The curse?

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:19.030
Sounds interesting.

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:22.330
If you're going to watch it, let me join you.

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:29.340
An inhuman monster
that stalks the streets at night...

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:33.460
Perhaps it's still out there
somewhere in Sakaimachi,

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:37.460
searching for its next victim.

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:45.100
So it's either a big carnivore cat,
a zombie, or maybe aliens.

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:47.060
That really narrows it down.

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:51.110
Right now, the fact that the
bodies were so badly damaged

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:52.980
makes most people think it was a big cat.

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:56.810
It was weird that they never covered
Principal Ryuzoji's mansion, though.

00:09:57.280 --> 00:09:59.450
That's where this whole
thing got started, right?

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:01.780
Yeah. That was really lazy of them.

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:05.050
You don't think they were worried
about character defamation?

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:09.120
I'm surprised you're
into this stuff, Eriko-<i>sensei</i>.

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:12.760
Women are drawn to things 
that are mysterious.

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:16.380
Be they crimes, or men...

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:24.010
"UFO Special, Ghost Special,
Psychic Powers Special, UMA Special (1),
UMA Special (2), Buried Treasure Special, Crop Circle Special, Seven Mysteries Special, Supernatural Phenomena Special"

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:24.010
All right, time for Masakatsu's
special selections!

00:10:24.420 --> 00:10:26.480
These are all masterpieces!

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:28.850
Boss, which one do we start with?

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:30.640
No, I...

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:34.430
Arima-<i>kun</i>, we need to talk.

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:36.320
Okay, sure.

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:37.740
Whew...

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:49.560
The swallows and sparrows know not
the thoughts of geese and swans.

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:57.460
You been busy lately?

00:10:57.590 --> 00:11:01.480
I'm spending every day going
through your father's research notes.

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:09.440
Hey, don't you think something's
changed with Ryuzoji-<i>sensei</i>, lately?

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:12.580
Yeah, I think he's acting weird.

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:14.050
I knew it...

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:16.030
Hey, Mitsuki-<i>san</i>.

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:20.360
Have you ever gotten a headache
when talking with Ryuzoji?

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:24.830
Sometimes, maybe...

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:31.170
It's possible he's using a type
of hypnosis called "Niarb" on you.

00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:33.420
Hypnosis?

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:38.260
When did you start
thinking he was acting weird?

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:40.530
Two months ago.

00:11:41.180 --> 00:11:42.430
I knew it.

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:45.100
That's when the curse started.

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:50.600
Nothing. I'll keep an eye on him.

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:52.230
Thanks.

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:56.820
There wasn't anybody else
I could talk to, so it's a huge help.

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:01.570
I have to go.

00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:03.160
I promised I'd meet him.

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:04.370
Will you make it in time?

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:07.990
Don't worry. It's the historical
research room, so it's close.

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:10.760
I have to be somewhere too.

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:12.400
See you later.

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:31.680
I guess this is the only place...

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:41.590
Eriko-<i>sensei</i>?

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:46.120
What are you doing?

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:48.700
That's my line!

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:50.160
Get out of there!

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:51.950
I can't do that right now!

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:53.980
But I need to use...

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:01.980
Is something wrong?

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:03.800
No.

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:07.090
This isn't meant for two people...

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:09.700
Just deal with it for a while.

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:11.810
Ichijo-<i>kun</i>,

00:13:12.120 --> 00:13:17.250
why don't you just come out
and tell me what it is that's been bothering you?

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:24.790
You've changed.

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:28.220
You're not who you were.

00:13:29.330 --> 00:13:31.740
Why do you think that?

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:35.870
It's hard to put into words, but...

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:42.630
But your mannerisms,
the way you move, your expressions...

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:46.520
You seem like a different person at times!

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:48.750
I see.

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:53.310
But if you'll allow me 
to speak in my defense,

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:58.480
the old you wouldn't have
said something like that.

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:03.460
Isn't it possible that you've changed,
instead of me?

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:08.450
The way you look at things. 
The way you think.

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:10.460
The way you understand. They've all changed.

00:14:11.090 --> 00:14:15.080
But instead of noticing that,

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:18.330
perhaps it seems to you like
the world around you has changed?

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:22.880
Perhaps you're simply lying to yourself?

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:26.380
I haven't changed...

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:30.730
But what if you were
the only one who felt that way?

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:37.750
Neither myself, nor my mother, have changed.

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:42.560
You're the one who's changed, Ichijo-<i>kun</i>.

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:44.140
That's impossible!

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:55.290
Hey, something hard's 
pressing up against me...

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:59.580
Well, that's just how men work...

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:02.330
And at a time like this...

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:05.380
Well, times like this are when it happens...

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:07.380
You don't need to let it worry you.

00:15:07.680 --> 00:15:10.340
It's a very natural thing.

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:16.640
Why did you change?
Why do you refuse to admit it?

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:22.290
I've noticed the hidden
feelings within you, Ichijo-<i>kun</i>.

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:27.030
Sensei...

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:30.030
I can't see, damn it.

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:31.360
What is he doing?

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:34.830
You've been holding back
because I'm married, right?

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:36.330
No, I...

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:42.670
Damn it! Mitsuki-<i>san</i>!

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:48.040
Forget about Mitsuki Ichijo.

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:50.880
What do you mean?

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:56.010
She's going to disappear soon.

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:10.300
Oww...

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:14.280
Mitsuki-<i>san</i> will disappear?
What does that mean?

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:16.070
What are your plans after this?

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:18.470
I'm very busy...

00:16:18.470 --> 00:16:20.370
No plans. Got it.

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:23.330
I'll see you at Cafe Evening
on Central Street.

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:24.580
What's this about?

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:27.740
There's something I want to show you.

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:36.970
Kanna-<i>chan</i>!

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:48.670
Someone who smells different.

00:16:49.730 --> 00:16:50.990
Ryuzoji?

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:52.270
Yes.

00:16:52.780 --> 00:16:55.220
He seems to want my necklace...

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:59.370
No, the stone itself.

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:02.560
Be careful, Arima-<i>san</i>.

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:30.580
Hey there.

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:41.120
Why are you dressed like that?

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:43.990
It's a disguise, obviously.

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:46.590
Look at that.

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:50.470
Ryuzoji and Kaori Asakura the journalist.

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:53.670
I should've known it wouldn't surprise you.

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:54.800
I guess not.

00:17:55.970 --> 00:17:57.620
How much do you know?

00:17:58.430 --> 00:17:59.930
I know most things.

00:18:01.260 --> 00:18:04.850
I guess that's what happens
if you keep doing it over and over again...

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:08.320
What about you?

00:18:09.060 --> 00:18:10.270
How much do you know?

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:13.070
I know most things.

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:17.780
That's all I wanted to make sure of.

00:18:17.780 --> 00:18:19.810
Now, let's head to our next destination.

00:18:20.800 --> 00:18:21.850
Where?

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:26.090
To see the cause of the curse.

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:35.880
Hey, you ever played catch?

00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:38.650
What's this got to do with anything?

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:42.850
Okay, catch!

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:46.390
Hey!

00:18:57.070 --> 00:19:00.490
Sorry. That one went wild.

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:02.010
That was definitely deliberate.

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:08.210
I'd better go in and get it back.

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:10.250
Now hurry.

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:19.610
So why are we trespassing into somebody's
house in the middle of the night?

00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:26.430
A certain woman has promised to
give me information on Principal Ryuzoji.

00:19:26.560 --> 00:19:27.790
A certain woman?

00:19:28.390 --> 00:19:29.600
Mitsuki-<i>san</i>?

00:19:29.600 --> 00:19:32.070
No. His mother.

00:19:33.040 --> 00:19:34.340
The old woman?

00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:37.890
I can hear it...

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:42.360
The breath of 400 years...

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:45.910
You sure there's any point in talking to her?

00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:49.290
She's just pretending to be senile.

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:50.870
You couldn't tell?

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:56.750
I think she figured out 
the principal's secret.

00:21:03.780 --> 00:21:05.970
That's his mom...

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:08.320
He wanted to keep her quiet, I'm sure.

00:21:11.750 --> 00:21:12.870
You won't get away!

00:21:12.870 --> 00:21:15.350
Hey! Are we just leaving her?

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:34.770
Oh no!

00:21:42.990 --> 00:21:46.090
Hey, what happened, Eriko-<i>sensei</i>?!

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:50.280
I hope she's okay, but...

00:21:57.250 --> 00:21:57.790
M-

00:21:58.790 --> 00:22:00.020
Mitsuki-<i>san</i>?

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:41.530
"Episode 13: An Ordained Fate"

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:39.170
Episode 13: "An Ordained Fate."
